  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Given that $\\sin\\theta=\\frac34$ and $\\theta$ is in Quadrant II, find each of the following:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac{3\\sqrt7}{8}$",
          "worked": "In Quadrant II, $\\cos\\theta<0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2\\theta&=1-\\left(\\frac34\\right)^2\\\\\\cos^2\\theta&=\\frac7{16}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac{\\sqrt7}{4}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin 2\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=2\\left(\\frac34\\right)\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt7}{4}\\right)\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=-\\frac{3\\sqrt7}{8}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac18$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos 2\\theta&=1-2\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=1-2\\left(\\frac34\\right)^2\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=1-\\frac{18}{16}\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=-\\frac18\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3\\sqrt7$",
          "worked": "In Quadrant II, $\\cos\\theta=-\\frac{\\sqrt7}{4}$, so $\\tan\\theta=-\\frac3{\\sqrt7}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{2\\left(-\\frac3{\\sqrt7}\\right)}{1-\\left(-\\frac3{\\sqrt7}\\right)^2}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{-6/\\sqrt7}{-2/7}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=\\frac{21}{\\sqrt7}\\\\\\tan 2\\theta&=3\\sqrt7\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
